cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SURF Test Unit: a low-cost 3-DOF motion phantom for surface-guidance QA"
message: "If you use this software, hardware design or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tim
    family-names: Buck
    # TODO before release: add orcid and confirm affiliation
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    affiliation: "Medical University of Innsbruck"
  # TODO before release: confirm co-author list and consent (see CONTRIBUTORS.md).
  # Contributors to the published history include S. Kollotzek (measurement data,
  # 2026-03-10 campaign) and A. M. Schneider (early control scripts).
repository-code: "https://github.com/tim-buck/SURF_ETD_QA"
abstract: >-
  Firmware, measurement software, hardware documentation and ground-truth
  measurement data for the SURF Test Unit: a three-degree-of-freedom motion
  phantom (horizontal slide, vertical slide, rotation, plus two heated pads)
  built to validate the tracking accuracy of a surface-guided radiotherapy
  system. The phantom logs commanded axis positions as ground truth; the
  companion analysis pipeline compares these against the tracking system's
  recorded pose.
keywords:
  - radiotherapy
  - surface-guided radiotherapy
  - SGRT
  - quality assurance
  - motion phantom
  - medical physics
# The repository is split-licensed and CFF cannot express that: a list here would
# mean "MIT OR GPL OR CC-BY". This field names the default licence of the
# software; firmware/ is GPL-3.0-or-later and data/ and docs/ are CC-BY-4.0,
# as set out under license-url.
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/tim-buck/SURF_ETD_QA/blob/main/README.md#licensing"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "SURF ETD analysis pipeline"
    authors:
      - given-names: Tim
        family-names: Buck
    repository-code: "https://github.com/tim-buck/SURF_DataAnalysis"
    notes: >-
      Companion repository. Holds the evaluation chain and the ExacTrac-side
      tracking exports. Neither repository alone contains a complete measurement.
